    "country": "US",
    "region": "New Jersey (statewide; NJ DOH OEMS approved, OETS adopted)",
    "emergencyNumber": "911"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "source": "State of New Jersey Emergency Medical Dispatch Guidecards (electronic edition, 'Updated May, 2026'; card footers Ver 01/16–02/16). Approved by the NJ Department of Health, Office of Emergency Medical Services; adopted by the NJ Office of Information Technology, Office of Emergency Telecommunications Services.",
    "url": "https://www.nj.gov/911/documents/resource/EMD%20Guidecards%202022%20elec%20proj%20Ebola.pdf",
    "license": "state-published-permission-pending",
    "digitizedDate": "2026-08-20",
    "notes": "Written-permission request tracked at AccesSOS/infra#8; the source PDF carries no copyright notice or terms, is published for free download, and is state-mandated for PSAPs (strong government-edicts posture), but state works are not automatically public domain — this pack ships under an explicit permission-pending marker until the reply lands. Digitized: All Caller Interrogation + CHEST PAIN/HEART PROBLEMS, CARDIAC ARREST/DOA, UNCONSCIOUS/FAINTING, UNKNOWN/PERSON DOWN (fallback), with NJ's own dispatch tiers (SIMULTANEOUS ALS/BLS, BLS DISPATCH, FOLLOW LOCAL PROTOCOL). Digitization decisions: (1) cross-card jumps (CPR cards, OD/POISONING, BREATHING PROBLEMS, AIRWAY CONTROL) are flattened into determinants — v0.1 cannot jump protocols mid-call; (2) the age criterion 'chest pain over 35' is not expressible (no numeric predicates), so chest pain defaults to SIMULTANEOUS ALS/BLS — age-unknown is treated as over 35, the safety-first reading, which makes the card's under-35 BLS tier unreachable in this digitization; (3) 'Determine age and sex of patient' is split into two scripted questions; (4) greeting, location/phone confirmations, dispatch confirmation, and closing are editorial (the cards do not script them); (5) the UNCERTAIN branch of 'Is the patient breathing NORMALLY?' is modeled as a third choice option that short-circuits to dispatch, per the card's flow to CPR/CARDIAC ARREST. SIMULATION ONLY — never for live call-taking. Schema v0.2 (2026-08-20): the All Caller flow's card jumps are modeled faithfully — an unconscious patient with abnormal/uncertain breathing routes to the CARDIAC ARREST/DOA card; the over/under-35 chest-pain tiers and single-faint-over-50 criterion are numeric age conditions (age unknown still defaults to the higher tier). Conscious callers with abnormal breathing dispatch directly: the BREATHING PROBLEMS card is not yet digitized. 2026-08-20 (2): added the BREATHING PROBLEMS card; per the All Caller chart, conscious patients with abnormal/uncertain breathing now route there (unconscious ones to CARDIAC ARREST/DOA). This card's ALS column reads 'any patient complaining of breathing or respiratory difficulty, examples may include...' — so it defaults SIMULTANEOUS_ALS_BLS; the BLS column (cold symptoms, stuffy nose, empty oxygen bottle, patient assist, long-term no change) describes benign presentations the schema cannot parse from free text and is unreachable in this digitization."
  },
